{"schema": "report-doc/1", "story": "diagnosis", "headline": "No configuration is shown to pass both gates: only the two with high reasoning and retry hold {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} in every task, and both run over the {criteria.p95.threshold} latency budget.", "lede": "Multi-hop lookups are every configuration's weakest task; the fastest near miss, Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry, falls short there by {criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.multihop.gap|abs} points. Per-task latency, never recorded, could open a routed mix and change the answer.", "recommends": [], "confidence": {"form": "high_if_immaterial", "caveats": [{"id": "no_control", "material_if": "Only for a claim that one configuration beats another: the call reads each configuration against the declared gates, and the setting effects are read unpaired, which errs wide rather than narrow."}, {"id": "best_of_n", "material_if": "Only where a configuration clears a gate by little. Brisk-S with high reasoning and retry clears multi-hop by {criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.high.r1.multihop.gap} points, best of {n_candidates|words}; a fresh run would likely read it lower, which strengthens rather than reverses the finding that nothing passes."}, {"id": "analyst:task-counts", "label": "Task pass rates state no case count", "material_if": "If Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry truly reaches the gate on multi-hop and ambiguous-entity lookups: its misses there are point estimates with no interval, so it could be a passer."}, {"id": "analyst:task-latency", "label": "Latency recorded only over all cases", "material_if": "Only for a routed mix nobody ran: if a high-reasoning configuration's tail latency within multi-hop lookups alone is inside the budget, sending only that task to it could clear both gates."}]}, "decision": [{"slot": "what_is_tangled", "text": "On multi-hop lookups the two gates pull against each other: only high reasoning with retry reaches {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} there, and both such configurations run over {criteria.p95.threshold} on tail latency. Ship none under the gates as declared."}, {"slot": "known_despite_it", "text": "Brisk-S with high reasoning and retry is the cheapest configuration that holds the pass rate in every task, at {cost_per_1k.brisk-s.high.r1} per thousand calls. Nano-XS reaches the gate in no task at any setting."}, {"slot": "watch", "text": "Brisk-S with high reasoning and retry clears multi-hop by only {criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.high.r1.multihop.gap} points, picked from {n_candidates|words} configurations, so a fresh run would likely read it lower. Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry misses {count.failing.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1|words} tasks narrowly and sits exactly on the line in date math; with no per-task counts those readings can't be told from noise."}, {"slot": "what_settles_it", "text": "Per-task tail latency: it decides whether any configuration, or a routed mix sending only multi-hop lookups to Brisk-S with high reasoning and retry, stays inside {criteria.p95.threshold} in each task it serves. If none does, the planner's owner has to say which gate gives way on multi-hop."}], "claims": [{"id": "c-gates", "weight": "lead", "text": "Only {count.passing.pass_rate|words} of the {n_candidates|words} configurations reach {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} in every task, both with high reasoning and retry; multi-hop lookups are the weakest task for every configuration.", "evidence": [{"block": "heatmap", "query": {"source": "tasks", "aspect": "", "measures": ["pass_rate"], "arms": [], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "reference": "floor", "caption": "Pass rate by task and configuration; cells under the {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} gate are outlined."}]}, {"id": "c-latency", "weight": "lead", "text": "Both run over the latency budget on tail latency across all cases: {measure.latency_ms.brisk-s.high.r1.p95} for Brisk-S and {measure.latency_ms.atlas-m.high.r1.p95} for Atlas-M, against {criteria.p95.threshold}. The gate reads each task and latency was kept only over all cases, so neither is formally failed, but a tail over budget across all cases means at least one task's tail is over it too.", "caveats": ["analyst:task-latency"], "evidence": [{"block": "range_bars", "query": {"source": "measures", "aspect": "", "measures": ["latency_ms"], "arms": [], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "reference": "budget", "emphasis": "brisk-s.high.r1", "caption": "Median to tail latency ({criteria.p95.statistic}) over all cases for each configuration, the {criteria.p95.threshold} budget marked."}]}, {"id": "c-nearest", "weight": "support", "text": "The configuration that comes closest inside the budget, Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry ({measure.latency_ms.brisk-s.low.r1.p95}), misses the pass-rate gate in {count.failing.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1|words} tasks: multi-hop by {criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.multihop.gap|abs} points and ambiguous entities by {criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.disamb.gap|abs}.", "caveats": ["analyst:task-counts"], "evidence": [{"block": "dot_interval", "query": {"source": "tasks", "aspect": "", "measures": ["pass_rate"], "arms": ["brisk-s.low.r1", "brisk-s.high.r1"], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "reference": "floor", "caption": "Per-task pass rate for Brisk-S with retry at low and at high reasoning, the gate marked; task rates state no case count, so no interval is drawn."}]}, {"id": "c-lever", "weight": "support", "text": "Between those two, moving from low to high reasoning adds {lever.reasoning.brisk-s.low.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.pass_rate.effect|abs} points overall, not separated from zero ({lever.reasoning.brisk-s.low.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.pass_rate.interval}); retry is the setting that separates at both reasoning levels.", "evidence": [{"block": "dot_interval", "query": {"source": "levers", "aspect": "", "measures": ["pass_rate"], "arms": ["brisk-s.low.r0", "brisk-s.low.r1", "brisk-s.high.r0", "brisk-s.high.r1"], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Overall pass-rate effect of each one-setting move among the Brisk-S configurations with low or high reasoning, and the reasoning step with retry less without, at {lever.reasoning.brisk-s.low.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.pass_rate.level} intervals read as independent."}]}, {"id": "c-cost", "weight": "detail", "text": "Of the two that hold the pass rate everywhere, Atlas-M costs {cost.gap.atlas-m.high.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.multiple} as much as Brisk-S, {cost.gap.atlas-m.high.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.monthly|abs} more a month, and Brisk-S's pass rate less Atlas-M's is not told apart from zero ({lever.model.atlas-m.high.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.pass_rate.interval}).", "evidence": [{"block": "bars", "query": {"source": "measures", "aspect": "", "measures": ["cost_per_1k"], "arms": ["atlas-m.high.r1", "brisk-s.high.r1", "brisk-s.low.r1"], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Cost per thousand calls for the two pass-rate passers and the nearest fast miss, on a log scale."}]}, {"id": "c-fail", "weight": "detail", "text": "The kept multi-hop failure of Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry merges two hops into one search; the date and ambiguous-entity cards fail other ways, an off-by-one window and a missing clarifying question.", "evidence": [{"block": "examples", "query": {"source": "examples", "aspect": "", "measures": [], "arms": ["brisk-s.low.r1"], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "The failures kept for this configuration, one per task where it failed; the input does not say how many failed in all."}]}], "explore": [{"control": "Latency budget", "binds": "Which configurations pass the latency gate in each task", "outcome": "No budget value changes the call: latency has no per-task figure, so the gate reads nothing at any threshold. Read over all cases instead, a budget at or above {measure.latency_ms.brisk-s.high.r1.p95} would admit Brisk-S with high reasoning and retry."}, {"control": "Pass-rate gate", "binds": "Which configurations hold the pass rate in every task", "outcome": "Lowering it admits more configurations on pass rate, Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry once it reaches {criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.multihop.value}, but no configuration passes both gates while latency has no per-task figure."}], "omitted": [{"what": "Overall pass rate per configuration", "why": "The gate reads each task; several configurations clear it overall yet miss multi-hop, so leading with it would mislead."}, {"what": "Calls per task and median latency", "why": "Neither bears on a declared gate."}, {"what": "Extra calls per task and outcome", "why": "The snapshot holds no figures for them."}, {"what": "Model and reasoning effects on Atlas-M and Nano-XS", "why": "They agree in direction with the Brisk-S effects shown; Nano-XS reaches the gate in no task, so its effects do not change the call."}, {"what": "Other thin pass-rate misses (Atlas-M high reasoning without retry on multi-hop, Brisk-S high reasoning without retry on date math)", "why": "Both configurations are over the latency budget across all cases, so settling their misses would not produce a passer."}, {"what": "Any cost or gain for a routed mix", "why": "Nobody ran one; it appears only as a next step."}], "next": [{"text": "Record tail latency per task for every configuration, from existing traces if kept, else by re-running.", "settles": "Whether any configuration, or a routed mix with Brisk-S high reasoning and retry on multi-hop only, stays inside the budget in each task it serves; a routed mix would then need its own run before shipping."}, {"text": "Re-run Brisk-S with low reasoning and retry on multi-hop and ambiguous-entity lookups, stating per-task counts. As a what-if, if each task held an equal share of today's cases, a run sized to settle most of the time needs {assumed.300.settle.criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.task.multihop.cases_needed_two_sided_80} multi-hop cases and {assumed.300.settle.criteria.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.task.disamb.cases_needed_two_sided_80} ambiguous-entity cases.", "settles": "Whether its misses are real or noise; if it truly reaches the gate there, it is a fast passer."}, {"text": "Improve multi-hop planning for Brisk-S at low reasoning, where the kept failure merges hops into one search, and re-run multi-hop.", "settles": "Whether a configuration inside the budget can reach the gate on multi-hop without high reasoning."}, {"text": "The planner's owner declares which gate gives way on multi-hop if no configuration passes both: a looser latency budget, or a lower pass-rate gate for that task.", "settles": "Turns the diagnosis into a decision: under a looser budget, Brisk-S with high reasoning and retry is the cheapest configuration that holds the pass rate."}], "method": [{"term": "Cases", "text": "{scoreboard.brisk-s.high.r1.cases} cases per configuration, with no repeats stated. The input does not say how cases split across tasks, only each task's share of traffic: {task.single.share} single lookups, {task.multihop.share} multi-hop, {task.datemath.share} date and unit math, {task.disamb.share} ambiguous entities."}, {"term": "Pass", "text": "The input does not define what makes a task pass; its failure classes are a missing call, wrong arguments and the wrong tool."}, {"term": "Gates", "text": "Pass rate at least {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} in each task, and tail latency ({criteria.p95.statistic}) at most {criteria.p95.threshold} in each task, both declared before the run. Latency was recorded only over all cases, so the latency gate has no figure in any task; a configuration with no failing figure is undecided, not failed."}, {"term": "Intervals", "text": "Setting effects carry {lever.reasoning.brisk-s.low.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.pass_rate.level} intervals from each configuration's binomial spread over its cases, combined as if independent, which reads wide if configurations shared cases. Per-task pass rates state no case count and carry none. There is no control, so nothing is paired, and no multiplicity correction applies."}, {"term": "Cost", "text": "Cost per thousand calls as measured. Monthly figures multiply it by the declared volume of {meta.volume_per_month}, and the input does not say what that volume counts."}, {"term": "Source", "text": "{meta.provenance}"}]}
```"}]}

